# Lesson 5, Sample B. New hand, opener's side.
title: Both majors, opener's side
id: L05-B
type: exercise
lesson: 5
concepts: 5.2, 5.6
student: S
board: 50
dealer: E
vulnerable: NS

deal:
  N  KJ62   Q5     A854   963
  E  53     T976   QJT92  54
  S  AQ74   KJ83   K6     A72
  W  T98    A42    73     KQJT8

auction:
  E Pass
  S 1NT*   = 15-17 points, balanced
     not *: 17 points and balanced: open 1NT.
  W Pass
  N 2C     = Stayman: do you have a 4-card major?
  E Pass
  S 2H*    = Four hearts (may also have four spades)
     key: Right: with both majors, bid hearts first.
     not 2S: With both majors, bid 2♥ first. If partner has spades, you'll still find out.
     not 2D: 2♦ says "no 4-card major." You have two.
  W Pass
  N 3NT    = Game values, but not four hearts
     key: Partner bid Stayman, so partner has a major. 3NT says it isn't hearts.
  E Pass
  S 4S*    = Four spades: we have a fit
     not Pass: Partner's major must be spades. Bid 4♠.
     not 4H: Partner's 3NT said "not hearts." Bid 4♠.
  W Pass
  N Pass
  E Pass

auction recap:
  With 17 points and a balanced hand, you open 1NT. Partner's 2♣ looks for a
  major. With both, you bid 2♥ first. Partner's 3NT says "not hearts, but
  game." Since Stayman promised a major, partner must have spades. You have
  them too: 4♠. South is declarer, because South bid spades first, and so West
  will lead to the first trick.

planning:
  trumps out: 5
  remind: What is the contract?

play:
  1   W CK  N C3  E C4  S CA
  2   S SA  W S8  N S2  E S3
      note: Draw trumps before the opponents can ruff a club.
  3   S S4  W S9  N SK  E S5
      note: Keep drawing trumps.
  4   N SJ  E D2  S S7  W ST
      note: Trumps are drawn.
  5   N H5  E H6  S HJ  W HA
      note: Knock out the ace of hearts.
  6   W CQ  N C6  E C5  S C2
  7   W CJ  N C9  E D9  S C7
      note: The defense has its three tricks.
  8   W CT  N D4  E DT  S SQ*
      SQ key: Ruff in hand, keeping dummy's last trump for a heart.
      SQ not H3: Did you notice you can ruff this club? Throwing a heart gives the defense a trick.
      SQ not DK: Did you notice you can ruff this club? Throwing a diamond gives the defense a trick.
      note: Ruff in hand, keeping dummy's last trump to ruff a heart.
  9   S H3  W H2  N HQ  E H7
      note: Lead a heart toward dummy's queen.
  10  N D5  E DJ  S DK  W D3
      note: Back to your hand with a diamond.
  11  S HK  W H4  N D8*  E HT
      D8 key: Keep the ace of diamonds; throw the 8.
      D8 not DA: Did you notice the ace is a sure trick? Discard the 8 instead.
      note: Dummy is out of hearts now.
  12  S H8  W C8  N S6  E H9
      note: Ruff the last heart in dummy.
  13  N DA  E DQ  S D6  W D7
      note: 10 tricks: 4♠ made.

play recap:
  The plan: draw trumps, knock out the ♥A, and ruff a heart in dummy for the
  extra trick.

  In 3NT, West leads ♣K. Declarer has only one club stopper and must knock
  out ♥A to make nine tricks. West wins it and cashes the clubs: four clubs
  and ♥A beat 3NT by one trick. In 4♠, the trumps stop the clubs and dummy's
  short hearts give an extra trick by ruffing. The 4-4 fit was worth a full
  game swing.
